## Failures

None high or medium.

### Low

1. Focus is dropped to the page when the panel is hidden from code while focus is inside it. Location: `src/components/sidebar/SidebarProvider.ts:85` (`open` change; only the viewport change at `:56` moves focus). Criterion: 2.4.3 Focus Order (best practice; the trigger is outside the panel, so no user action causes it). Verified: focused "Installation", set `provider.open = false`, `document.activeElement` became `body`; the next Tab did land on the trigger because Chromium keeps its sequential starting point. Fix: in `updated()`, when `open` turned false and focus was inside the sidebar, focus the trigger, as the viewport handler does. Not a blocker.
2. A group whose label is removed keeps `role="group"` with an empty name. Location: `src/controllers/labelled-by.ts:37`. Criterion: 1.3.1 / 4.1.2 (a group with no label is noise, not a barrier). Verified: removed the first group label, AX shows `group ""`. Fix: not needed when a label is optional by design (contract allows it); if desired, drop the role when no label is found.

Observations, not failures:
- Wide Tab order puts the trigger after the panel links by DOM order (documented in the spec's "Tab order" coverage); a keyboard user passes six links to reach it. Acceptable under 2.4.1 with the `nav` landmark, but a skip link is the team's call.
- Tab wrap inside the drawer relies on `FOCUSABLE` plus `delegatesFocus` (`Sidebar.ts:10`); slotted custom controls without delegated focus are skipped as first or last. Recorded in the contract's known drift.

