## Initial assessment

Semantics, real keyboard behavior in the wide panel and the modal drawer (open, Tab wrap both ways, Escape, link close, focus return), the new `LabelledByController` group names (live, dynamic, no ID crossing shadow roots), 24px targets, contrast and focus ring in light and dark, forced colors, reduced motion, reflow, RTL, axe, S1, the 53/53 behavior spec and `check` all pass. Only two low findings and a stale contract.md line pair remained; the initial call was ready.

## Status (2026-11-16, after fixes)

Re-verified live in Chromium against Storybook (real key presses, CDP AX tree):
- Low 1 closed: with focus on "Installation", `provider.open = false` from code moves focus to the trigger (`SidebarProvider.ts` willUpdate/updated, `#refocus`); Enter on the trigger reopens the panel.
- Low 2 closed: removing a group's label leaves no group role and no empty-named group in the AX tree (`SidebarGroup.ts:34` `#syncRole`); a label added later restores `role=group` named "Back"; an author `aria-label` names the group "Author"; an author role is kept by design.
- Stale contract.md lines closed: `contract.md` frontmatter says `status: beta` and the Figma section says it is drawn and read back.
- `tests/sidebar`: 55 passed (53 plus the two new tests).

Nothing remained open at that point.

## Status (2026-11-16, after the second round)

Re-verified live in Chromium with real key presses (Storybook on 6117); `tests/sidebar` 58 passed.

Passing:
- Shortcut, wide: Control+B and Meta+B each toggle the panel off and on; Shift+ and Alt+ variants are ignored; `collapsible=none` ignores it (panel stays open, key not consumed). With focus on a panel link, Control+B closes the panel and focus moves to the trigger; pressing it again reopens.
- Typing guard: with focus in an `<input>`, a `<textarea>` and a `contenteditable` div, Control+B and Meta+B leave `open` unchanged (the key keeps meaning bold).
- Trigger: `aria-keyshortcuts="Control+B Meta+B"` present on the inner button (`SidebarTrigger.ts:40`).
- Shortcut, narrow: Control+B opens the drawer (focus on the first link); Meta+B closes it; Escape still returns focus to the trigger.
- Drawer wrap (`src/utils/focus-wrap.ts`): 8 Tabs cycle the six links and wrap with no escape; Shift+Tab from the first wraps; unchanged from round one.

Open finding, MEDIUM: after the drawer is closed with the shortcut, focus does not return to the trigger as the contract says (`contract.json` aria, drawer entry), so it lands on whatever held focus before opening. Location: `src/components/sidebar/SidebarProvider.ts:120-124` (`#closeDrawer` focuses `#opener`) racing `src/components/sidebar/Sidebar.ts:47` (`dialog.close()` runs afterwards in `updated()` and the browser restores focus to the element focused before `showModal()`, overriding it). Criterion: 2.4.3 Focus Order. Verified with fresh pages, open with Control+B then close with Control+B: nothing focused before gives `body`; focus on "Back to top" gives that link; only focus already on the trigger gives the trigger. Escape after a shortcut open is correct (the `close` event fires after the native restore). Fix: focus the opener after the dialog has closed, for example in `Sidebar.ts` `updated()` right after `dialog.close()` call the provider's opener focus (or move the `#opener.focus()` into the `close` handler path), and add a spec step that opens the drawer by shortcut with focus elsewhere and expects the trigger after the shortcut close. The same ordering also affects closing by an activated link if the drawer was opened without the trigger holding focus (for example by the shortcut, or a click in a browser that does not focus buttons on click).

## Status (2026-11-16, third round)

The MEDIUM focus-return finding is closed (`SidebarProvider.ts` `#closeDrawer` now waits for the native dialog to close before focusing the opener). Re-verified live with real key presses: with nothing focused and with focus on "Back to top" before opening by Control+B, focus ends on the trigger after each of: Control+B close, Enter on an activated menu link, Escape, and a click on the backdrop. The trigger-driven flows (Enter then Escape, backdrop, Control+B) still return to the trigger. `tests/sidebar` 59 passed. Nothing remains open.

Verdict: ready
